note SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT OR GPL-2.0-only
note seq: check a GSP-RM "run CPU sequencer" request completely before the kernel performs any of it.
note GSP-RM sends a list of register operations the host must run (kgspExecuteSequencerBuffer,
note kernel_gsp.c:5297, open-gpu-kernel-modules 580.173.02; opcodes and payload sizes rmgspseq.h
note GSP_SEQUENCER_PAYLOAD_SIZE_DWORDS). This unit reads the whole received message, refuses anything
note malformed, and writes a normalized list of operations; the kernel glue then performs the list.
note Oracle: aien-dev/aienux c9678d7b native/kernel/gpu/gsp_seq.c (tests/host/parity_seq.c).
note Difference from the oracle and from NVIDIA, on purpose: the whole buffer is checked first, so a bad
note entry anywhere refuses before the first register write; every register offset must be 4-byte
note aligned and inside BAR0 (barlen); at most 2048 operations.
note
note msg: the message as agpu_mq_get returned it: 48-byte element header, 32-byte RPC header whose
note length field (offset 56) counts header plus payload, then rpc_run_cpu_sequencer_v17_00:
note bufferSizeDWord at 80, cmdIndex at 84, regSaveArea[8] at 88, commandBuffer[] at 120.
note ops: 6 ulong per operation: opcode, then up to 5 payload dwords (unused ones 0).
note Opcodes: 0 REG_WRITE (addr val), 1 REG_MODIFY (addr mask val), 2 REG_POLL (addr mask val timeout
note error), 3 DELAY_US (us), 4 REG_STORE (addr index), 5..8 CORE_RESET/START/WAIT/RESUME (no payload).
note Result: the number of operations (0..2048), or 1000000 plus a refusal code:
note 1 message too short for the request header, 2 bufferSizeDWord is 0, 3 buffer longer than the message,
note 4 cmdIndex not inside the buffer, 5 unknown opcode, 6 opcode payload overruns cmdIndex,
note 7 REG_STORE index 8 or more, 8 register offset unaligned or outside BAR0, 9 more than 2048 operations.
fn rd32 msg view uchar 65536 o ulong to ulong
a = or ulong get msg o shl ulong get msg add o 1 8
b = or shl ulong get msg add o 2 16 shl ulong get msg add o 3 24
ret or a b
end
fn paydw op ulong to ulong
if eq op 0
ret 2
end
if eq op 1
ret 3
end
if eq op 2
ret 5
end
if eq op 3
ret 1
end
if eq op 4
ret 2
end
if le op 8
ret 0
end
ret 99
end
fn regok a ulong barlen ulong to bool
if ne and a 3 0
ret false
end
ret le add a 4 barlen
end
note Check one operation's payload (p = byte offset of its first payload dword) and copy it to ops.
fn seqop msg view uchar 65536 p ulong op ulong ops edit ulong 12288 k ulong barlen ulong to ulong
base = mul k 6
put ops base op
n = paydw op
for j ulong 5
v = ulong 0
if lt j n
v = rd32 msg add p mul j 4
end
put ops add base add j 1 v
end
if and le op 4 ne op 3
if not regok get ops add base 1 barlen
ret 8
end
end
if and eq op 4 ge get ops add base 2 8
ret 7
end
ret 0
end
fn agpu_seq_check msg view uchar 65536 ops edit ulong 12288 barlen ulong to ulong
rlen = rd32 msg 56
if lt rlen 72
ret 1000001
end
nw = rd32 msg 80
cmdi = rd32 msg 84
if eq nw 0
ret 1000002
end
if gt add 120 mul nw 4 add 48 rlen
ret 1000003
end
if ge cmdi nw
ret 1000004
end
i = ulong 0
k = ulong 0
while lt i cmdi bound 16384
op = rd32 msg add 120 mul i 4
i = add i 1
n = paydw op
if eq n 99
ret 1000005
end
if gt add i n cmdi
ret 1000006
end
if ge k 2048
ret 1000009
end
e = seqop msg add 120 mul i 4 op ops k barlen
if ne e 0
ret add 1000000 e
end
k = add k 1
i = add i n
end
ret k
end
